continuation:
To terminate a C program, you can use the `exit()` function. Here's an example of how to use it:
```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, world!\n");
    exit(0); // Terminate the program
    return 0;
}
```

When you run this program, it will print "Hello, world!" to the console and then terminate.<|im_end|>
